.TH tuwc n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuwc
.PP
\fBtclutils::tuwc\fR counts lines, words, characters and bytes.
.SS Load
.CS
package require tclutils::tuwc
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuwc::text data
::tclutils::tuwc::file filename
.CE
.SS Result
.PP
Both commands return a dictionary:
.CS
lines 10 words 42 chars 180 bytes 190
.CE
.PP
The \fBfile\fR command additionally adds the key \fBfile\fR.
.TS
l l.
Key	Meaning
\fBlines\fR	number of \fB\en\fR, plus one when the text does not end in \fB\en\fR
\fBwords\fR	runs of non\-whitespace
\fBchars\fR	characters (code points)
\fBbytes\fR	\fBtext\fR: length in UTF\-8; \fBfile\fR: size of the file in bytes
.TE
.PP
\fBlines\fR differs from \fBwc \-l\fR: a last line without \fB\en\fR counts. An empty text has 0 lines, \fB"\en"\fR has one.
.PP
\fBfile\fR reads with the system encoding and turns \fB\er\en\fR into \fB\en\fR; \fBlines\fR, \fBwords\fR and \fBchars\fR count that text. \fBbytes\fR is the file size on disk, as with \fBwc \-c\fR.
